<title>USA: Northrop Grumman sells Astrotech unit.</title>
<headline>Northrop Grumman sells Astrotech unit.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northrop Grumman Corp said Thursday it agreed to sell its Astrotech unit to SPACEHAB Inc.</p>
<p>Terms of the sale, which is expected to close later this month, were not disclosed. Astrotech provides payload processing services for commercial satellites at a center near the Kennedy Space Center in Florida and at another facility near Vandenberg Air Force Base in California. It employs 18 people and had revenues in 1996 of about $8 million.</p>
</text>
